  "id": "animal-physiology",
  "title": "How Animals Work: Comparative Physiology",
  "summary": "An audio-first comparative investigation of how animals maintain their internal conditions, move, and sense their surroundings: regulation, gas exchange, circulation, water balance, digestion, muscles, neural signaling, touch, proprioception, hearing, vision, chemoreception, electroreception and thermal sensing. The course compares multiple animal lineages and continues toward temperature, hormones, defense and reproduction.",
